// Adds style:display-name when the style's name in the document is not the one it has in the file, as for "Heading 1" written "Heading_20_1"; the default style, written "Standard", gets none, because LibreOffice would then keep "Standard" and add a second style called "Normal" beside it.
odt_package_display_name(XmlW odt_package_display_writer, string odt_package_display_document_name, string odt_package_display_file_name) {
